TITLE:: CompressorSidechainSource
summary:: where the sidechain page's spectrum reads
categories:: Libraries>Compressor
related:: Classes/CompressorPanel, Classes/ParaEQSpectrum

DESCRIPTION::
What a ParaEQSpectrum asks an eq, answered for what a compressor's detector
listens to, before its eq: the input - read just before the compressor's own
node, or at the end of a driven proxy's group (what leaves it: there is no way
in) - or the sidechain bus, read at the tail of the default group. A
SuperDirtGUI orbit's busses are written inside SuperDirt's group, which sits
before that tail. The graph's own sidechain (code::sidechain = true::) has no bus
to read, so there is no picture rather than a wrong one.

code::
c = Compressor.new;
t = CompressorSidechainSource(c);
t.analysisAvailable;      // false: no node, no bus
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: comp

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: comp
METHOD:: server
METHOD:: enabled
METHOD:: analysisPlacement
RETURNS:: [target, addAction], or nil
METHOD:: analysisBusIndex
METHOD:: analysisChannels
